(ARM Architecture Overview: ARM microcontrollers utilize a memory-mapped architecture where peripherals) Tj
T* (\(like GPIO, Timers, UART\) are assigned specific memory addresses. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (GPIO Configuration: To control a pin, we must first configure its mode \(Input/Output/Alternate Function\) using) Tj
T* (the Mode Register \(MODER\). We achieve this by reading the register, applying a bitwise mask to clear the) Tj
T* (relevant bits, and using an OR operation to set the new mode.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Bit Set/Reset: Rather than writing directly to the Output Data Register \(ODR\) which requires a) Tj
T* (read-modify-write cycle, modern ARM chips provide a Bit Set/Reset Register \(BSRR\) that allows atomic,) Tj
T* (thread-safe pin toggling in a single clock cycle.) Tj
ET
